An [[Unidentified wattled species|alien]] '''individual''' served as [[Oathkeeper]] of the [[Imperial Senate]] of the [[Galactic Empire]] during its [[Imperial Era|reign]].<ref name="Festive" /> In [[3 BBY]],<ref name="Date">"[[Ever Been to Ghorman?]]" dates the events of "[[What a Festive Evening]]" to [[3 BBY]].</ref> they led a session of the senate in an oath of allegiance during [[Senate Investiture]] [[Standard week|week]], crying out from<ref name="Festive" /> the [[Chancellor's Podium]] in the [[Imperial Senate Building]] on the [[planet]] [[Coruscant]].<ref name="CLNE">''[[Star Wars: Complete Locations, New Edition]]''</ref> The [[senator]]s present repeated each line of the oath after the Oathkeeper and cheered once it was complete, although Senator [[Mon Mothma]] stopped repeating the Oathkeeper's words before they finished.<ref name="Festive" /> In [[2 BBY]],<ref name="MessengerDate">{{Andor|Messenger}} dates the third arc of [[Andor Season 2|''Andor'' Season 2]] to [[2 BBY]].</ref> the Oathkeeper initiated a Senate meeting, where [[Mon Mothma]] spoke out about the [[Ghorman Massacre]], publicly denounced [[Supreme Chancellor]] [[Darth Sidious|Palpatine]] and revealed herself as a member of the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebellion]].<ref name="Welcome Rebellion">{{Andor|Welcome to the Rebellion}}</ref>

==Personality and traits==
While leading the oath, the Oathkeeper wore [[Color|brown]] and golden [[Clothing|robes]] and a piece of golden headwear. They had brown skin and brown [[eye]]s.<ref name="Festive" />

==Behind the scenes==
The Oathkeeper first appeared in "[[What a Festive Evening]]," the sixth episode of the [[Andor Season 2|second season]] of the [[Disney+]] live-action series ''[[Star Wars: Andor]]'',<ref name="Festive" /> which aired on [[April 29]], [[2025]].<ref name="Trailer News">{{SW|url=news/andor-season-2-teaser-trailer-key-art-reveal|text=First ''Andor A Star Wars Story'' Teaser Trailer and Poster Revealed}}</ref> The Oathkeeper was portrayed by [[Cavin Cornwall]].<ref name="Festive" />

